+Analysis-only diagnostics for base 49d6b76, ATL 4cbbe2f (126 examples).
+The patch changes no retention model or rule. DISTILL_TRIM_PREFIX enables sidecar
+model/AST/reference/inventory/copy-map diagnostics. Apply the patch only temporarily.
+
+All paths are worktree-local except the explicitly allowed read-only ATL clone.
+Use TMPDIR="$PWD/.checks/trim/tmp" for every command; create that directory first.
+Run the example stages sequentially. Each stage uses at most two examples.
+
+SDK acquisition (before applying diagnostics, if reproducing the clean baseline):
+ GITHUB_REPOSITORY=jcg9129/cpp-distill timeout 600 python3 ci/llvm/acquire.py \
+   --source release --version 23.1.5 --rev 1 --platform linux-arm64
+The acquisition verifies public release SHA256SUMS. Expected archive SHA-256:
+5ca712f18c710592a8fa89758246a6b6cbdbd16c1fbd5f12c7f5bcdf35fe06de
+ timeout 120 cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+   '-DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE=-O1 -DNDEBUG' -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang \
+   -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++ -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS=-fuse-ld=lld \
+   -DDISTILL_LLVM_DIR="$PWD/spike-work/sdk/lib/cmake/llvm"
+ timeout 900 cmake --build build --parallel 2
+Copy distill and distill_prune_worker to .checks/trim/baseline before applying patch.
+After applying diagnostics, rebuild with a 600-second cap and --parallel 2.
+Never edit a source file while a compiler is reading it.
+
+Cross packages: timeout 600 python3 .checks/trim/acquire-cross.py
+Every .deb is verified against SHA256 from public Ubuntu questing package indexes.
+The g++ wrapper uses the relocated native AArch64-hosted x86_64 GCC 15.2 compiler.
+QEMU executes standalone outputs using the worktree-local x86_64 runtime.
